      "content": "Cut Edge (Bridge)"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "A bridge is a specific edge that, when removed, results in a disconnected graph."
    },
    {
      "type": "image",
      "alt": "A Graph With a Bridge",
      "src": "data:image/png;base64,"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "In the figure above, the edge connecting the vertices 0 and 4 is a bridge because removing it will result in two distinct graphs. However, removing any other edge will still result in a single graph."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Thus, a bridge serves as a critical point in the network's structure, and its removal can break the network into separate components."
    },
